  "id": "irrelevant-language",
  "term": "irrelevant language",
  "definition": "Irrelevant language refers to a language or language variety that is not needed for the current task but may still become mentally active while a person is listening or speaking. In this context, it means non-target language forms that can be co-activated even when someone is meant to use a different language or variety.",
